# shell-env_example — shell environment sourced before each wake firing.
#
# Copy to "shell-env" in the kanban root and edit:
#
#   cp shell-env_example "$PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH/shell-env"
#
# Put PATH adjustments, virtualenv activation, and any other non-secret
# shell environment here. For sensitive credentials (OAuth tokens, API
# keys), use "secrets" instead — see secrets_example.
#
# Who sources it:
#   - Every wake firing (wake-batch.sh / wake/claude.sh / wake/codex.sh)
#     sources it, always, through the wake bootstrap.
#   - Other entry points (po-agent.sh, pm-agent.sh, overwatch-sweep.sh,
#     cleanup, the dashboard and operator scripts) source it through
#     scripts/lib/env_bootstrap.sh ONLY when PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH is
#     not already set in their environment. The crontab templates export
#     that variable, so a cron-launched po-agent, pm-agent, overwatch-sweep
#     or cleanup runs WITHOUT this file's PATH and virtualenv: put what they
#     need into the crontab's own PATH line as well.
#   - pseudocron.py does not source it; its jobs get their environment from
#     pseudocron.py's own environment plus pseudocron.env.
#
# Notes:
#   - This file is OPTIONAL — wake scripts work without it as long as the
#     launching environment provides a usable PATH. The kanban root is
#     derived from each script's own location when
#     PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH is unset.
#   - The file is shell-sourced — any syntax error halts the wake firing.
#     Test edits with: bash -n $PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH/shell-env
#   - For wake-loop tunables (max_tasks_per_wake, etc.), edit kanban.cfg
#     [wake] instead. For per-agent model overrides, edit kanban.cfg
#     [models.<provider>] (e.g., [models.claude], [models.codex]) — the
#     active provider is resolved from [providers] active at wake startup.
#     This file is shell-only — no INI translation happens here.
#
# All lines below are commented out by default. Uncomment to use.


# --- Kanban root ---
# PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH — the kanban installation every script acts
# on. Read by every entry point (scripts/lib/env_bootstrap.sh, the Python
# ops layer).
# Default: derived from the running script's own location (the directory
# above scripts/), so it is normally left unset. The crontab templates
# export it explicitly; set it here only to point every non-cron entry
# point at a different install.
# KANBAN_ROOT is the legacy alias: the Python ops layer still honours it,
# ahead of PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH, when it is set. No default (unset).
#
# export PGAI_AGENT_KANBAN_ROOT_PATH="$HOME/pgai_agent_kanban"


# --- PATH ---
# Cron jobs run with a minimal PATH and won't find tools in $HOME without
# this. Uncomment if `claude` or `codex` CLIs aren't on the default cron PATH.
# Read by the shell that sources this file (see "Who sources it" above).
# Default: not modified (uses whatever PATH the launching environment provides)
# export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$HOME/bin:$PATH"


# --- Python virtualenv (optional) ---
# Activate a Python virtualenv if your system Python is too old.
# The kanban requires Python 3.12+; the wake scripts refuse to start on an
# older interpreter.
# No default — leave commented unless system Python is unsuitable.
# source "$HOME/py3.12/bin/activate"
